  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I’d like to propose adding a new built-in parameter: EyeHeightAsMetersInverse (calculated as 1 / EyeHeightAsMeters).\n\nUse Case:\n\nThis would be extremely useful for scaling logic within BlendTrees, where division operations are not natively supported.\n\nFor example, if a creator wants to calculate a scale relative to a specific distance (e.g., \"How many 'avatar heights' are in 10 meters?\"), the formula is 10 / EyeHeightAsMeters. Currently, this is difficult to implement. With EyeHeightAsMetersInverse, we can simply use a multiplication node: 10 × EyeHeightAsMetersInverse, making complex scaling logic much more accessible.",
